<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The round launcher icon: the same three layers as ic_launcher.xml.

  Separate because `android:roundIcon` is a separate manifest attribute and some
  launchers ask for it by name, not because the artwork differs – an adaptive icon is
  already masked to whatever shape the launcher wants, so pointing both at the same
  layers is correct and keeps them from drifting.

  Three layers, not a bitmap for the whole icon: the launcher masks background and
  foreground to its own shape and parallaxes them, and <monochrome> is what lets Android
  13+ tint the icon to the user's wallpaper instead of dropping a coloured square into a
  themed home screen.

  ## Why the foreground is a bitmap

  Same reason it was one for the CoralX mark it replaces: the artwork is supplied, not
  ours to draw. The Coral Telecom lockup is type plus a four-colour swoosh with soft
  shading, and tracing that would ship something that is nearly the brand, which is worse
  than shipping the brand. So it ships as PNGs at all five densities, generated from the
  supplied file with its white ground keyed to transparency, and the plate behind it is
  white so the dark type reads and the keyed edges cannot seam.

  ## The one thing to know before reusing this

  The source, docs/brand/coral-telecom-logo.jpeg, is 187x148. The mark inside it trims to 175x135, and the largest
  layer this icon needs is 288x222 – so xxhdpi and xxxhdpi are UPSCALED, by about 1.2x
  and 1.6x. It is sharp enough on a launcher and it is not sharp enough for a 512px Play
  Store listing or a 1024px iOS icon. Replacing the source with a square, transparent
  PNG of at least 1024px, or the original vector, is the fix; regenerating from a bigger
  file is the only step, since nothing here is hand-tuned to these pixels.

  Every layer is 108dp with the mark inside the 66% the launcher is guaranteed to keep,
  which is what stops a circular mask from cutting the ends off the lockup.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
